.TH SCALA 1 "2026" "scalars 0.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scala \- Scala as a fusevm frontend (bytecode VM + Cranelift JIT, no JVM)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scala
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR] [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scalars
lexes and parses Scala and lowers it to
.B fusevm
bytecode executed on a three\-tier Cranelift JIT.
There is no bespoke VM and no JVM; execution and codegen live in fusevm,
the same engine behind zshrs, stryke, awkrs, elisp, rubylang, and pythonrs.
.PP
The program text is a single
.B .scala
file whose entry point is an
.B object
that either
.B extends App
(its body runs directly) or declares
.BR "def main(args: Array[String]): Unit" .
It supports
.BR val / var
bindings,
.BR if / while
and every
.B for
form,
.BR println / print ,
and the arithmetic, comparison, and boolean operators, with faithful
.BR Int -vs- Double
division dispatch, String
.B +
concatenation, structural
.BR == ,
and Java
.B Double.toString
formatting.
User\-defined methods (including block\-local ones), classes, objects,
.BR "case class" es,
traits with inheritance and virtual dispatch,
.BR try / catch / throw ,
first\-class and partial functions, and the collection library
.RB ( List ,
.BR Seq ,
.BR Vector ,
.BR Set ,
.BR Map ,
.BR Array ,
.BR Range ,
and the
.B scala.collection.mutable
buffers, sets and maps) are carried too, each reproducing Scala's own
iteration order.  Regular expressions are
.BR java.util.regex :
.BR matches ,
.BR replaceAll ,
the regex\-based
.BR split ,
and
.BR \(dq\&...\(dq.r
with the
.B scala.util.matching.Regex
surface.  For the gaps that remain \(em
.B Char
as its own type, lazy views,
.BR Iterator ,
.BR LazyList ,
user
.BR Ordering s,
and the wider standard library \(em see
.B BUGS.md
in the source tree.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-tokens
Print the lexer token stream for the file and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-ast
Print the parsed AST for the file and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-tiers
Run it, then report which fusevm execution tier took each of its chunks.
.TP
.B \-\-disasm
Print a fusevm bytecode disassembly listing for the file and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-lsp
Speak the Language Server Protocol over stdio (completion, hover, live
parse diagnostics).
.TP
.B \-\-dap
Speak the Debug Adapter Protocol over stdio (source\-line breakpoints,
stepping, stack/scopes/variables).
.TP
.BR \-version ", " \-\-version
Print the version banner and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the option grammar and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion.
.TP
.B 1
Error during lexing, parsing, lowering, or execution.  Errors are written
to stderr as
.BR "scalars: <reason>" .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run a Scala file:
.RS
.nf
scala hello.scala
.fi
.RE
.PP
Disassemble the lowered bytecode:
.RS
.nf
scala --disasm hello.scala
.fi
.RE
.PP
Start the language server / debugger over stdio (for an editor):
.RS
.nf
scala --lsp
scala --dap
.fi
.RE
